1hx5|n|The act of obeying, or the state of being obedient; compliance with that which is required by authority; subjection to rightful restraint or control. ; Words or actions denoting submission to authority; dutifulness. ; A following; a body of adherents; as, the Roman Catholic obedience, or the whole body of persons who submit to the authority of the pope. ; A cell (or offshoot of a larger monastery) governed by a prior. ; One of the three monastic vows. ; The written precept of a superior in a religious order or congregation to a subject.	a:8vn,100,4~8vn,100,4
